<article class="env-lemma" id="063R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/063R">Lemma <span data-tag="063R">31.23.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $i : Z \subset X$ be an immersion. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$i$ is an $H_1$-regular (resp. quasi-regular) immersion, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$Z \to S$ is a flat morphism. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then for every morphism of schemes $g : S' \to S$ the base change $Z' = S' \times _ S Z \to X' = S' \times _ S X$ is an $H_1$-regular (resp. quasi-regular) immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Unwinding the definitions and using Lemma <a href="/tag/063G" data-tag="063G">31.21.7</a> this translates into More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CEP" data-tag="0CEP">15.32.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>